A sign-up application as cybertrain v0.4.1's generators wrote it, kept so
that test/cli_authentication_upgrade.rb and `script/auth-e2e upgrade04`
can re-run today's `generate authentication` over a 0.4 application
(the upgrade path, D19 of the phase 4b plan).

Tag: v0.4.1 (commit d8a9825). Produced once, on 2026-11-12, with:

  git worktree add $TMP/v041 v0.4.1
  cd $TMP
  export CYBERTRAIN_TIMESTAMP=20260925120000
  ruby -I$TMP/v041 $TMP/v041/exe/cybertrain new shop --path ../..
  cd shop
  ruby -I../v041 ../v041/exe/cybertrain generate authentication
  git worktree remove $TMP/v041

`new` then tried to bootstrap (spin lock, spin run gen) against ../..,
which holds no framework from $TMP, and stopped there: gen/ has only its
.keep, as `new` wrote it, and that is what is kept. Every file is as
written, except:

  * build/ (the empty build directory of the failed bootstrap) is left out;
  * tmp/.keep is left out (the repository's .gitignore ignores tmp/);
  * spin.toml and spin.lock name the framework as path "../../.." (the
    repository root, seen from this directory) in place of the absolute
    path `new` wrote. script/auth-e2e points a copy at the checkout it
    tests.

Nothing under this directory is a test of the framework: test/*.rb here
are the application's own, run only by script/auth-e2e upgrade04.
